---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '~/lib/site';

/**
 * Master Services Agreement — supplied as a signed-off legal template
 * (MASTER_SERVICES_AGREEMENT_TEMPLATE.docx), converted to this page
 * essentially verbatim. Deliberately NOT in Header/Footer/menu.ts nav —
 * a direct link to share with prospects/clients, not a discoverable page.
 * noindex + excluded from the sitemap filter in astro.config.mjs for the
 * same reason.
 *
 * FLAGGED, not filled in: the source document is a TEMPLATE with several
 * unresolved placeholders — no Provider legal entity name, [DATE],
 * [CLIENT], the Acceptable Use Policy URL (www.__________), the Initial
 * Term length (_______(X) years), and the notice email
 * (clientnotice@Provider.com). Those are reproduced below exactly as
 * blanks/brackets rather than guessed at. This also has not yet been
 * through the legal review the 7/31 meeting flagged as an open action
 * item (Speaker 2) — treat this as a working draft link, not a
 * ready-to-sign document, until that review happens and the blanks are
 * filled in (ideally per-engagement via the actual Order Form process
 * described in Section 1, not hardcoded here).
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Master Services Agreement"
  description="AllTech's Master Services Agreement template."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="surface-dark py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <header class="mb-10">
        <div class="eyebrow mb-4">Legal</div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight" style="color: var(--color-text-primary);">
          Master Services Agreement
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-text-subtle);">
          This is a template. Provider, Client, dates, term length, and a few other
          fields below are still unfilled pending an executed Order Form for a specific engagement.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-alltech legal-body">
        <p>
          This Master Services Agreement (&ldquo;Agreement&rdquo;) is made and entered into as of
          [DATE] (the &ldquo;Effective Date&rdquo;) by and between ___________ (&ldquo;Provider&rdquo;)
          and [CLIENT] (&ldquo;Client&rdquo;). Provider and Client are referred to herein individually
          as a &ldquo;Party&rdquo; and collectively as the &ldquo;Parties.&rdquo; In consideration of
          the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein and for other good and valuable
          consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties
          hereby agree as follows:
        </p>

        <h2 id="services">1. Services</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>1.1 Order Forms.</strong> Prior to Provider&rsquo;s provision of a Service to Client
          (for the purposes of this Agreement &ldquo;Service(s)&rdquo; shall be defined as those
          certain services as set forth on the Order Form(s)), the Parties will execute: (i) for
          Standard Services, a Service Order Form (&ldquo;SOF&rdquo;); and (ii) for Professional
          Services, a Statement of Work (&ldquo;SOW&rdquo;) (SOFs and SOWs may be collectively or
          individually be referred to as &ldquo;Order Form(s)&rdquo; as context may require). Each
          Order Form will specifically describe the Services to be provided and any applicable terms
          and conditions and service levels. Upon execution by both Parties, each Order Form will
          become part of and subject to this Agreement. Changes to an Order Form shall be made in a
          writing executed by authorized representatives of both Parties (a &ldquo;Change Order
          Form&rdquo;). Any Order Forms that predate the execution of this Agreement shall remain in
          full effect, and in the event of conflicting terms in any Order Form and this Agreement, the
          terms in the Order Form shall control, as applicable.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>1.2 Third Party Service Providers.</strong> Except as otherwise set forth in an
          applicable Order Form, Client acknowledges that portions of the Services may be provided by
          third parties. Client agrees to Provider&rsquo;s use of such third parties as necessary to
          provide the applicable Services. Client further agrees to enter into any additional terms
          and conditions and other agreements with such third parties as may be reasonably necessary
          in connection with Provider&rsquo;s provision of the Services to Client.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>1.3 Acceptable Use Policy.</strong> Client&rsquo;s use of the Services, in addition
          to all requirements set forth in this Agreement and the applicable Order Form(s), shall be
          in accordance with the Provider Acceptable Use Policy available at www.__________, as well
          as all Provider operating manuals, user manuals, training materials, guides, product
          descriptions, specifications, technical manuals, supporting materials, policies or other
          information relating to the Services published by Provider and/or as provided or otherwise
          made available to Client from time-to-time, whether in electronic form or otherwise (the
          &ldquo;Documentation&rdquo;).
        </p>

        <h2 id="client-responsibilities">2. Client Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>2.1 Provision of Equipment.</strong> Except as otherwise set forth in the applicable
          Order Form(s), Client shall be responsible for obtaining and maintaining any equipment and
          ancillary services needed to connect to, access, or otherwise make use of the Services,
          including, without limitation, modems, hardware, servers, software, operating systems,
          networking equipment, web servers and the like (collectively, the &ldquo;Equipment&rdquo;).
          Client shall also be responsible for maintaining the security of the Equipment, Client
          account usernames and passwords (including, but not limited to, administrative and user
          passwords) and files, and for all uses of the Equipment or Client accounts with or without
          Client&rsquo;s knowledge or consent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>2.2 Security Requirements.</strong> Client shall: (i) only access the hardware,
          networks, systems or applications owned and/or operated by Provider or otherwise made
          available to Client by Provider (collectively, the &ldquo;Provider Systems&rdquo;) as
          permitted under this Agreement and the applicable Order Form and/or as otherwise authorized
          by Provider in writing; (ii) maintain up-to-date operating system patching and active
          anti-malware on all end-user devices used to connect to Provider Systems; (iii) ensure that,
          in the event Client terminates the employment of, or otherwise revokes permissions to access
          the Provider Systems on Client&rsquo;s behalf, any employee or other authorized end user,
          Client disables their access to the Provider Systems within twenty-four (24) hours of
          termination or revocation; (iv) notify Provider within seventy-two (72) hours of security
          incidents that could impact Provider; and (v) ensure Client&rsquo;s users keep user IDs and
          passwords used to access the Provider Systems confidential at all times. Client shall be
          responsible for compliance with all applicable laws and privacy policies in its use and
          receipt of the Services, including but not limited to, its use and storage of any personal
          data, as that term is commonly known in the industry, through or in connection with the
          Services.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ownership">3. Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>3.1 Services.</strong> As between the Parties, except as otherwise provided herein,
          Provider owns all right, title and interest in and to the Services, including any
          improvements, modifications, enhancements, additions and derivatives thereof and any and all
          Intellectual Property Rights in all of the foregoing. Client does not acquire any rights,
          express or implied in the foregoing other than those specified in this Agreement. Provider
          shall retain all right, title and interest in and to all Provider intellectual property,
          including all rights therein.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>3.2 Client Data.</strong> With respect to the Cloud Services, as between the Parties,
          Client shall own all right, title and interest in and to any applications, information,
          materials and other data stored and otherwise utilized by Client in connection with the
          Cloud Services (the &ldquo;Client Data&rdquo;). Client hereby grants to Provider a limited,
          revocable, non-transferable, royalty-free license to reproduce, translate, encode, publish,
          use and distribute the Client Data for the purpose of providing the Cloud Services to
          Client.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>3.3 Client Marks.</strong> If and to the extent any Services include utilizing any
          marks of Client (&ldquo;Client Marks&rdquo;), Client hereby grants to Provider a limited,
          non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable, royalty-free license to use the Client Marks
          solely for the limited purposes of the performance of this Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>3.4 Aggregate Data.</strong> Notwithstanding anything to the contrary herein,
          Provider shall have the right to compile, collect, copy, modify, publish and use anonymous
          and aggregate data generated from or based on Client&rsquo;s use of the Services
          (collectively, &ldquo;Aggregate Data&rdquo;) for analytical and other business purposes.
          Provider shall use commercially reasonable efforts to ensure Client is not, and will not, be
          identified as the source of any Aggregate Data. As between the Parties, Provider owns all
          right, title and interest in and to the Aggregate Data, including all Intellectual Property
          Rights therein, irrespective of whether such Aggregate Data contains any anonymized or
          aggregated Client Data. For clarification, Aggregate Data shall be limited to only data that
          is generated from or based on Client&rsquo;s use of the Services, and Provider shall only
          use Aggregate Data for the purposes of monitoring and improving the performance of the
          Services or its overall operations.
        </p>

        <h2 id="term">4. Term and Termination</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>4.1 Term.</strong> This Agreement shall be effective upon the Effective Date and,
          unless terminated earlier as set forth herein, shall remain in full force and effect for a
          period of _______(X) years (the &ldquo;Initial Term&rdquo;). This Agreement shall
          automatically renew at the end of the Initial Term for successive renewal terms of one (1)
          year (each, a &ldquo;Renewal Term&rdquo;) unless either Party gives the other Party written
          notice of its intent not to renew this Agreement at least ninety (90) days prior to the
          expiration of the Initial Term or the then-current Renewal Term. The Initial Term along with
          any and all Renewal Terms is referred to herein as the &ldquo;Term.&rdquo; For any Order Form
          still in effect at the expiration or, if applicable, earlier termination of this Agreement,
          the terms of this Agreement shall remain in full force and effect with respect to such Order
          Form until such Order Form expires or is terminated in accordance with this Agreement and/or
          the terms contained in such Order Form; provided that the duration of any such Order Form
          may not be extended after the expiration or, if applicable, earlier termination of this
          Agreement. In the event of conflicting terms in any Order Form and this Agreement, the terms
          in the Order Form shall control, as applicable.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>4.2 Termination.</strong> In addition to a Party&rsquo;s rights to terminate this
          Agreement as set forth elsewhere in this Agreement, either Party may terminate this
          Agreement and/or any outstanding Order Form upon any of the following events effective upon
          notice from the terminating Party:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            If the other Party makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors or if the other Party
            ceases to do business or otherwise terminates its business operations, other than after an
            assignment which is permitted by the terms of this Agreement;
          </li>
          <li>
            If the other Party becomes insolvent, or voluntary or involuntary proceedings are
            instituted by or against such other Party under any federal, state or other bankruptcy or
            insolvency laws, and, in the case of proceedings commenced against such Party, such
            proceedings are not terminated within sixty (60) days, or a receiver is appointed for such
            other Party; or
          </li>
          <li>
            If the other Party fails to perform any material provision of this Agreement: (i) and such
            failure is incapable of being cured; (ii) if such failure relates to Client&rsquo;s failure
            to pay Fees when due, Client fails to remedy such failure within ten (10) days after
            receiving notice of such failure from Provider; or (iii) for all other failures that are
            capable of being cured, the other Party does not cure such failure within a period of
            thirty (30) days after receipt of notice from the other Party reasonably specifying such
            failure, or if such failure cannot reasonably be cured within such thirty (30) day period,
            the other Party fails to: (1) promptly commence to remedy such failure; (2) continuously
            and diligently pursue the remedy of such failure; and (3) cure such failure within a period
            of sixty (60) days after receipt of the notice of failure (or such other time period as
            agreed upon by the Parties).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>4.3 Suspension.</strong> Notwithstanding the foregoing termination provisions set
          forth herein, Provider may, immediately and without notice to Client, suspend the provision
          of the Services, in whole or in part, or terminate this Agreement and/or an applicable Order
          Form, subject only to an opportunity to cure as set forth in Section 4.2(c), for the
          following: (i) any Fees or Expenses remain unpaid thirty (30) days after the applicable due
          date; (ii) providing the Services is prohibited by law; or (iii) Client&rsquo;s use of the
          Services are in violation of this Agreement, the applicable Order Form, the Documentation
          and/or applicable law.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>4.4 Effect of Termination.</strong> Termination of this Agreement will not terminate
          any applicable Order Form, and the terms of such Order Form shall control, including but not
          limited to, the fees and termination provisions included on the Order Form.
        </p>

        <h2 id="payment">5. Payment</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>5.1 Fees.</strong> Client will pay Provider all undisputed invoiced fees for Services
          as detailed in the applicable Order Form (&ldquo;Fees&rdquo;) and invoiced expenses, without
          deduction or setoff. Except as otherwise expressly provided in the applicable Order Form, for
          any Services provided on an hourly basis, all time shall be billed in one-quarter hour (i.e.,
          15 minute) increments. Provider reserves the right to increase any and all Fees, in its
          reasonable judgment, provided such Provider shall not increase any Fee more than once in any
          six (6) month period. For clarity, the foregoing limitation shall not apply to any changes or
          other modifications to Fees set forth in any Change Order Form. Notwithstanding the
          foregoing, with respect to any Fees included in an Order Form that include fees passed by or
          through a third party (&ldquo;Third Party Fees&rdquo;), Provider cannot guarantee that such
          Third Party Fees will remain the same for the duration of the applicable Order Form. In the
          event any Third Party Fees are increased, Provider may proportionately adjust the applicable
          Fees upon written notice to Customer.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>5.2 Invoices.</strong> Unless otherwise set forth in an Order Form, Provider will
          invoice Client on a monthly basis. All undisputed Fees and Expenses are due and payable, in
          US dollars, within thirty (30) days of the date of the applicable invoice. Any payments made
          via credit or debit card may be subject to an additional four percent (4%) surcharge. Without
          prejudice to its other rights and remedies under this Agreement, including the applicable
          Order Form(s), or at law or in equity, in the event Client fails to pay any amount due and
          payable by Client under this Agreement by the due date, in addition to the other rights under
          this Agreement, Provider may charge interest at the lesser of a monthly rate of one and
          one-half percent (1.5%) of the unpaid amount or the maximum amount permissible by law, and
          such interest will accrue on a daily basis from the date the relevant payment is due until
          payment in full is received. Client further agrees to pay all of Provider&rsquo;s costs of
          collection of unpaid amounts due hereunder, including reasonable attorneys&rsquo; fees.
        </p>

        <h2 id="confidentiality">6. Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>
          Each Party will use reasonable care to prevent the unauthorized use or dissemination of the
          other Party&rsquo;s confidential information. Confidential information is limited to
          information clearly marked as confidential, disclosed orally and summarized and identified
          as confidential in a writing delivered to the other within thirty (30) days of such
          disclosures, or is or should be known to the receiving Party or a reasonable person given the
          facts and circumstances of the disclosure, as being treated as confidential or proprietary by
          the disclosing Party. The terms of this Agreement shall be the confidential information of
          both Parties. Confidential information of the disclosing Party does not include information
          that the receiving party can establish: (1) the other knew before it was disclosed; (2) is or
          becomes public knowledge through no fault of the other; (3) is obtained from other sources
          who owe no duty of confidentiality to the other; or (4) is developed independently (as
          demonstrated by the written files or records of the receiving Party). Each Party agrees to
          inform its respective employees and contractors by contract to maintain as confidential each
          other&rsquo;s confidential information. The Parties agree that the non-breaching Party will
          be entitled to seek injunctive or other extraordinary relief, in any case of any such breach
          or threatened breach in order to prohibit such breach or threatened breach and to command
          compliance with this Agreement, without posting a bond or other security.
        </p>

        <h2 id="warranties">7. Representations, Warranties and Covenants; Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>7.1 General.</strong> Each Party represents and warrants to the other Party that: (i)
          such Party has the full right, power, and authority under its governing documents to enter
          into this Agreement and perform its respective obligations; (ii) the execution of this
          Agreement by such Party and the performance of its obligations in accordance with this
          Agreement do not and will not violate any agreement which such Party is a party or by which
          it is otherwise bound; (iii) when executed and delivered by such Party, this Agreement will
          constitute the legal, valid, and binding obligation of such Party, enforceable against such
          Party in accordance with its terms; and (iv) its performance under this Agreement shall be in
          compliance with all Applicable Laws.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>7.2 Third-Party Products.</strong> Products manufactured by a third party
          (&ldquo;Third-Party Product&rdquo;) may constitute, contain, and/or be contained in,
          incorporated into, attached to, packaged together with, or provided in conjunction with the
          Services or other Provider deliverables. Provider makes no representations or warranties
          with respect to any Third-Party Product.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>7.3 Disclaimer.</strong> PROVIDER DOES NOT REPRESENT OR WARRANT THAT THE SERVICES
          WILL BE ERROR-FREE OR UNINTERRUPTED. EXCEPT IN THE INSTANCE OF GROSS NEGLIGENCE OR WILLFUL
          MISCONDUCT BY PROVIDER, CLIENT ASSUMES THE ENTIRE RISK AS TO THE USE OF THE SERVICES IN TERMS
          OF CORRECTNESS, ACCURACY, RELIABILITY, CURRENTNESS OR OTHERWISE. This disclaimer of
          warranties does not, in any way, affect the terms of any applicable warranties provided by
          the manufacturer of a Third-Party Product.
        </p>

        <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>8.1 General.</strong> IN NO EVENT SHALL EITHER PARTY BE LIABLE TO THE OTHER PARTY
          UNDER THIS AGREEMENT FOR ANY INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY OR
          PUNITIVE DAMAGES (EVEN IF PREVIOUSLY APPRISED OF THE POSSIBILITY THEREOF), WHETHER THE BASIS
          OF THE LIABILITY IS A MATERIAL BREACH OF CONTRACT, TORT (INCLUDING GROSS NEGLIGENCE AND
          STRICT LIABILITY), STATUTORY OR ANY OTHER LEGAL THEORY OR FOR ANY ERROR OR INTERRUPTION OF
          USE, LOSS, INACCURACY OR CORRUPTION OF DATA COST OF PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS, SERVICES
          OR TECHNOLOGY OR LOSS OF PRODUCTIVITY. THE AMOUNT OF PROVIDER&rsquo;S LIABILITY TO CLIENT
          UNDER ANY AND ALL CLAIMS FOR LOSS OR LIABILITY BASED UPON, ARISING OUT OF, RESULTING FROM OR
          IN ANY WAY CONNECTED WITH PROVIDER&rsquo;S PERFORMANCE OR BREACH OF THIS AGREEMENT SHALL IN
          NO CASE EXCEED THE FEES ACTUALLY PAID BY CLIENT TO PROVIDER HEREUNDER IN THE SIX (6) MONTHS
          PRECEDING THE ACT GIVING RISE TO THE LIABILITY.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>8.2 Exclusions.</strong> THE FOREGOING LIMITATIONS OF LIABILITY SHALL NOT APPLY WITH
          RESPECT TO ANY OF THE FOLLOWING: (i) A PARTY&rsquo;S BREACH OF ITS CONFIDENTIALITY
          OBLIGATIONS; (ii) A PARTY&rsquo;S INDEMNIFICATION OBLIGATIONS; (iii) A PARTY&rsquo;S BREACH OF
          ANY REPRESENTATION, WARRANTY OR COVENANT MADE HEREUNDER; OR (iv) ANY DAMAGES RESULTING FROM A
          PARTY&rsquo;S NEGLIGENCE OR WILLFUL MISCONDUCT. FOR THE SAKE OF CLARITY, AND NOTWITHSTANDING
          ANYTHING TO THE CONTRARY HEREIN, PROVIDER SHALL NOT BE RESPONSIBLE OR LIABLE UNDER THIS
          AGREEMENT FOR ANY COSTS, EXPENSES, DAMAGES OR LIABILITIES, AND CLIENT SHALL BEAR ALL
          RESPONSIBILITY WITH RESPECT TO ANY DAMAGES OR LIABILITIES CAUSED BY OR ARISING FROM: (i) ANY
          VIOLATION OF ANY APPLICABLE LAW OR ANY THIRD PARTY CLAIM ASSOCIATED WITH THE CLIENT DATA;
          (ii) THE ACTION OR INACTION OF CLIENT (UNLESS SUCH PARTICULAR ACTION OR INACTION WAS TAKEN OR
          NOT TAKEN AT THE SPECIFIC DIRECTION OF PROVIDER); OR (iii) CLIENT&rsquo;S FAILURE TO FULFILL
          ITS RESPONSIBILITIES HEREUNDER.
        </p>

        <h2 id="indemnification">9. Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>9.1 Mutual.</strong> Each Party (an &ldquo;Indemnifying Party&rdquo;) hereby
          indemnifies, defends and holds harmless the other Party and its Affiliates, and its and their
          officers, directors, employees, agents and attorneys (&ldquo;Indemnified Parties&rdquo;) from
          and against any and all losses, settlements, claims, actions, suits, proceedings,
          investigations, judgments, awards, damages and liabilities (collectively,
          &ldquo;Losses&rdquo;), and shall reimburse the Indemnified Parties for any and all legal
          (including reasonable attorneys&rsquo; fees), accounting, and other fees, costs and expenses
          reasonably incurred in connection with any such Loss (collectively, &ldquo;Costs&rdquo;),
          which Losses or Costs are sustained by, or asserted against, any Indemnified Party and arise
          out of: (i) Indemnifying Party&rsquo;s breach of its representations, warranties and
          covenants hereunder; (ii) Indemnifying Party&rsquo;s acts or omissions (including negligence
          and strict liability and including any injury to any person (including but not limited to
          death) or property) in connection with the subject matter of this Agreement, including,
          without limitation, any violation of Applicable Law; (iii) Indemnifying Party&rsquo;s
          violation or alleged violation of any term of this Agreement; or (iv) any claim that the
          Indemnifying Party infringes or engages in a wrongful use of any third party&rsquo;s
          Intellectual Property Rights, any right of publicity or privacy, libel or defamation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>9.2 Additional Remedies.</strong> Without limiting Provider&rsquo;s foregoing
          indemnification obligations, in the event of any claim of infringement, or if Provider
          becomes aware of any impending Claim of Infringement, Provider may, at its option and
          expense: (i) procure for Client, at no cost to Client, the right to continue to use the
          affected Services; (ii) replace or modify the affected Services, at no cost to Client and
          with no adverse effect on the operation, performance, features or functionality or services
          of such Services, to eliminate the Claim of Infringement; or (iii) if Provider determines in
          its sole discretion that the foregoing solutions are not practical or economically feasible,
          Provider may terminate the applicable Order Form(s) and refund to Client any Fees paid for
          the affected Services which have been prepaid but unused.
        </p>

        <h2 id="notices">10. Notices</h2>
        <p>
          Any notice given hereunder shall be sent via email to the other Party&rsquo;s email address
          set forth herein or on an Order Form or to such other party and email address as such Party
          shall most recently have designated. Such notice shall be deemed given on the date of the
          return receipt email. Any notice to Provider shall be sent via email to
          clientnotice@Provider.com or to such other email address Provider shall most recently have
          designated.
        </p>

        <h2 id="misc">11. Miscellaneous</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>11.1 Relationship of the Parties.</strong> The relationship of Client and its
          successors in interest, on the one hand, and Provider and its successors in interest, on the
          other hand, is that of independent contractors, and not one of principal and agent, joint
          venture or partnership.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>11.2 Binding Effect.</strong> This Agreement shall be binding on and inure to the
          benefit of the Parties and their respective permitted successors and assigns. Provider may
          assign its rights and delegate its duties under this Agreement (in whole or in part) without
          Client&rsquo;s consent to any Affiliate or in connection with a merger, consolidation, sale
          of all or substantially all of its assets, other business combination, spin-off or other
          restructuring. Client may not assign any of its rights or delegate any of its duties under
          this Agreement (by operation of law or otherwise) without Provider&rsquo;s prior written
          consent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>11.3 Non-Solicitation/Non-Interference.</strong> During the Term, and for a period of
          twelve (12) months thereafter (the &ldquo;Non-Solicitation Period&rdquo;), Client shall not
          directly or indirectly solicit or hire, or induce or encourage to leave employment with
          Provider, any employee of Provider that was employed by Provider during the Non-Solicitation
          Period unless such individual has no longer been employed with Provider for a period of six
          (6) months at the time of the solicitation (&ldquo;Restricted Candidates&rdquo;).
          Notwithstanding the foregoing, it shall not be a violation of this non-solicitation provision
          for Client to place general advertisements, job postings or other general solicitations not
          targeted at Restricted Candidates; provided that Client may not make any offers of employment
          to or hire Restricted Candidates responding to any such solicitation. In the event Client
          breaches this Section 11.3 and either (i) hires a Restricted Candidate or (ii) solicits
          and/or attempts to hire a Restricted Candidate such that Provider incurs costs in retaining
          such Restricted Candidate, Client agrees to pay Provider as liquidated damages (and not as a
          penalty) one hundred fifty thousand dollars ($150,000) in the event of a breach of the hiring
          restriction, or such lesser amount as deemed appropriate by Provider in the event of a breach
          of the non-solicitation restriction. Client acknowledges and agrees that this amount is an
          effort by Provider to properly and reasonably assess the damages that would be suffered as a
          direct result of the breach of this Section 11.3 by Client, or any of Client&rsquo;s
          Affiliates or subsidiaries, taking into account the fact that Provider will lose significant
          revenue and incur significant costs and will have to expend significant time and effort in
          connection with attempts to recruit, train and replace any such employee. In light of these
          circumstances, Client agrees that these liquidated damages provision represents reasonable
          compensation to Provider for the losses that it would incur due to any such breach. This
          Section 11.3 shall survive the expiration or earlier termination of this Agreement for any
          reason for a period of twelve (12) months.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>11.4 Force Majeure.</strong> Neither Party is responsible for delays or failures in
          performance resulting from acts of God, strikes, lockouts, riots, acts of war and terrorism,
          embargoes, changes in governmental regulations, epidemics, fire, communication line failures,
          power failures, earthquakes or other disasters (each, an event of &ldquo;Force
          Majeure&rdquo;). Neither Party is entitled to relief under this Section 11.4 to the extent
          that any event otherwise constituting an event of Force Majeure results from the negligence
          or fault of the Party claiming relief from performance.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>11.5 Survival.</strong> The rights and obligations of the Parties set forth in this
          Agreement that by their nature are intended to survive the expiration or earlier termination
          of this Agreement — including, but not limited to, Sections 6, 8, and 9 — shall survive the
          expiration or earlier termination of this Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>11.6 Entire Agreement; Amendment.</strong> This Agreement, including any Exhibits and
          documents referred to in this Agreement or attached hereto, including, without limitation,
          the Documentation, and each Order Form executed by the Parties, constitutes the entire and
          exclusive statement of this Agreement with respect to its subject matter and supersedes any
          and all oral or written representations, understandings or agreements relating thereto.
          Without limiting the foregoing, the Parties agree that this Agreement supersedes any prior
          master services agreement or other similar agreement between the Parties or any of their
          predecessors-in-interest except as otherwise agreed between the Parties in writing
          (&ldquo;Prior Agreement&rdquo;) and, unless otherwise agreed in writing between the Parties,
          any and all such Prior Agreements are hereby terminated as of the Effective Date. This
          Agreement may be modified, supplemented or changed only by an agreement in writing which
          makes specific reference to this Agreement and which is signed by both Provider and Client;
          provided, however, notwithstanding the foregoing, Provider shall have the right to modify the
          Documentation and any and all Acceptable Use Policies upon thirty (30) days&rsquo; prior
          written notice to Client.
        </p>
        <p>
